# 7. I would introduce a domain concept: `VotingEntitlement`

This is the part I would emphasize more strongly than the report.

Currently the real voting entitlement is hidden inside:

```text
User::isVoterInElection()
```

and:

```text
EnsuresVoterMembership
```

The investigation correctly identifies these as the existing enforcement choke points. Eingefügter Text

Architecturally, however, the business concept is bigger than "is this user a member?"

It is:

> **Does this person currently possess the right to cast a ballot in this election?**

That deserves a named domain concept.

For example:

```text
VotingEntitlement
```

or:

```text
ElectionVotingEntitlement
```

Then:

```text
VotingEntitlement.canCastVote(
    election,
    voter
)
```

evaluates:

```text
ElectionMembership
        │
        ├── registered?
        │
        └── active?
                │
                ▼
        AdmissionPolicy
                │
                ├── Gate 1
                ├── Gate 2
                └── ...
                │
                ▼
        Exercisability
                │
                ▼
        ElectionLifecycle
                │
                ▼
            CAN VOTE
```

That gives us a **single domain boundary for the most important security invariant**.

