# 12. Constitution vs Election Policy

Here I would be careful because your repository already has an architectural ruling.

The investigation found that the existing ruling says voter-participation rules should remain outside `ElectionConstitution::RULES` unless a new ADR changes that decision. Eingefügter Text

Therefore I would **not yet call the new object `ElectionConstitution.voterGates`**.

Instead:

```text
Election
   │
   ├── Constitution
   │
   ├── VoterSourceStrategy
   │
   └── VoterAdmissionPolicy
```

Conceptually:

```text
ElectionConstitution
    = constitutional election rules

VoterAdmissionPolicy
    = who must pass which admission requirements

VotingEntitlement
    = whether the voter may exercise the right now
```

This is a cleaner bounded-context separation.

---

# 13. My proposed aggregate responsibility

I would make `Election` the owner of the **admission policy**.

Not the organisation.

Not the voter.

Not the global configuration.

Because the requirement is:

> "For this election, what must an imported voter satisfy?"

Therefore:

```text
Election
 └── VoterAdmissionPolicy
```

is appropriate.

But the **evidence** belongs to the voter/election relationship:

```text
Election
   │
   └── ElectionMembership
            │
            └── VoterVerification
```

This produces:

```text
RULE
Election → VoterAdmissionPolicy

EVIDENCE
Election + Voter → VoterVerification

DECISION
Election + Voter → VotingEntitlement
```

That is a very clean DDD separation.

