# 14. I would make the policy immutable at the right moment

The investigation recommends creation-time fixation. I agree with the principle, but I would make the lifecycle explicit.

### Election creation

```text
Draft
   ↓
Administration
```

Admission policy can be selected.

### Administration

Potentially:

```text
Admission Policy
    can be configured
```

but changing it should create an explicit protocol/audit event and show impact.

### Election becomes locked

Once the election enters the legally/operationally relevant phase:

```text
Admission Policy
       ↓
IMMUTABLE
```

The exact transition should be decided by the election lifecycle—not merely by a database column.

