# 17. The security invariant

Ultimately everything should reduce to one authoritative rule:

```text
CanCastVote(voter, election)
```

must return `true` only if:

```text
1. Election exists
2. Voter belongs to this election
3. Voter has voter role
4. Membership is not removed
5. Membership is exercisable
6. All required admission gates have passed
7. Election is currently votable
8. Existing ballot-security rules pass
9. Voter has not already voted
```

Importantly:

```text
UI
 ──┐
API ├──→ VotingEntitlement
CLI ┤
Job ┘
```

All roads must eventually hit the same entitlement decision.

The current system already has a useful enforcement choke point, which is why the investigation's proposed minimal implementation is attractive. Eingefügter Text

