## The most important conceptual result

I would put this sentence into the Publicdigit architecture documentation:

> **Importing a voter registers an election-specific voting entitlement candidate; it does not necessarily grant the right to exercise the vote. Admission is determined by the election's voter-admission policy and its required gate evidence. Voting entitlement is the final domain decision that combines registration, admission, exercisability and the election lifecycle.**

That gives us a much stronger foundation than simply adding a "verified" flag.

And it resolves the central flaw found in the current implementation: **today `active` effectively means registered + admitted + allowed to vote, while the existing Verify operation is merely recorded and has no effect on eligibility.** Eingefügter Text

The next architectural artifact I would create is therefore **“Publicdigit Voter Admission & Eligibility Domain Model v0.1”**—with the aggregate boundaries, invariants, lifecycle/state model, admission-gate model, constitution/policy boundary, and sequence diagrams—**before writing the implementation ADR**.